{{template "head" .}}
<section class="hero">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="spacer">
      <div class="copy">
        <h1>NSM Hosting</h1>
        <p>Run your own city on our servers. The official server software is installed for you, your ports are assigned automatically, and everything is managed from your hosting dashboard.</p>
        <div class="btnpadder">
          <a class="btn primary" href="/hosting/create">Create a server</a>
          <a class="btn" href="/hosting/manage">Manage my server</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="container">
    <div class="spacer">
      <hr>
      <h1>One package. For everyone.</h1>
      <p>No tiers, no add-ons, no confusing choices — every NSM Hosting customer receives the same standard server package.</p>
      <div class="fx">
        <div class="c-lg-6 c-md-6 c-xs-12">
          <table class="stat-table">
            <tr><td class="stat">Package</td><td>{{.PKG.Name}} — free</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="stat">Player slots</td><td>{{.PKG.Slots}}</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="stat">Memory</td><td>{{.PKG.RAMGB}} GB RAM allocation</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="stat">Storage</td><td>{{.PKG.DiskGB}} GB for your server files</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="stat">Ports</td><td>{{.PKG.Ports}} reserved ports (game TCP + UDP, files, extras)</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="stat">Software</td><td>Official NSM server, installed automatically</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="stat">Included</td><td>Live console, file manager, FileZilla access, private join link</td></tr>
          </table>
        </div>
        <div class="c-lg-6 c-md-6 c-xs-12">
          <h2>The hardware</h2>
          <p>Your city runs on the NSM hosting node. The specifications below are read from the actual machine at runtime — we do not advertise numbers we cannot verify.</p>
          <table class="stat-table">
            <tr><td class="stat">Host CPU</td><td>{{if .CPUModel}}{{.CPUModel}}, {{end}}{{.Cores}} cores</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="stat">Host memory</td><td>{{if .RAMText}}{{.RAMText}}{{else}}reported at runtime{{end}}</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="stat">Isolation</td><td>Each server has its own directory, files and ports</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="stat">Port pool</td><td>{{.First}}–{{.Last}} (500 ports, TCP and UDP)</td></tr>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="container">
    <div class="spacer">
      <hr>
      <h1>Live in three steps</h1>
      <div class="fx">
        <div class="c-lg-4 c-md-4 c-xs-12">
          <article class="a1"><h2>1. Create</h2><span class="txt">Sign in with your NSM account and create your server. One server per account.</span></article>
        </div>
        <div class="c-lg-4 c-md-4 c-xs-12">
          <article class="a2"><h2>2. Install</h2><span class="txt">The official server files are downloaded and installed into your server's own directory, with your ports written into <code>server.cfg</code>.</span></article>
        </div>
        <div class="c-lg-4 c-md-4 c-xs-12">
          <article class="a3"><h2>3. Manage</h2><span class="txt">Start and stop the server, use the live console, edit files and share your private join link — all from the dashboard.</span></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="container">
    <div class="spacer">
      <hr>
      <h1>Your dashboard</h1>
      <div class="fx">
        <div class="c-lg-3 c-md-6 c-sm-6 c-xs-12">
          <article class="a1"><h2>Console</h2><span class="txt">Real-time server output and commands, exactly as the process reports them.</span></article>
        </div>
        <div class="c-lg-3 c-md-6 c-sm-6 c-xs-12">
          <article class="a2"><h2>Files</h2><span class="txt">Browse, edit, upload and download your actual server files on the VPS.</span></article>
        </div>
        <div class="c-lg-3 c-md-6 c-sm-6 c-xs-12">
          <article class="a3"><h2>Ports</h2><span class="txt">Every port assigned to your server, with its purpose and live status.</span></article>
        </div>
        <div class="c-lg-3 c-md-6 c-sm-6 c-xs-12">
          <article class="a4"><h2>Overview</h2><span class="txt">Status, uptime, CPU, RAM and disk usage, and start/stop/restart controls.</span></article>
        </div>
      </div>
      <h2 class="closing">Ready? <a href="/hosting/create">Create your server</a>.</h2>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
{{template "foot" .}}
